{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>חשף.</b> The meaning: He bared His arm, like a mighty warrior who slays with the strength of his arm." "<b>כל אפסי ארץ.</b> Some say: the ends of the earth, without a connective vav, only from context. Others said it is like ואשור באפס עשקו (Isaiah 47:8), as if to say 'in its end'; and similarly אני ואפסי [above, Isaiah 4]. Some say the alef is added, like פיסת בר (Psalms 72:16). The correct view in my eyes is that it is like מי אפסי. Do not wonder that the verse places hand and foot and belly and mouth [upon HaShem]; the principle is known: the speaker is a human being and so is the listener. He casts the words by way of metaphor, as though they pertain to the form of a human being, so that the listeners may understand."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 52, :notes {1 "The bracketed [above, Isaiah 4] likely refers to a cross-reference within Isaiah; exact verse uncertain from this witness."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:13.148520444Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}